<concept id="t00339">
	<title>OFF mode</title>
	<prolog>
		<metadata>
			<keywords>
				<indexterm>automatic climate control system 
					<indexterm>off mode</indexterm>
				</indexterm>
			</keywords>
		</metadata>
	</prolog>
	<conbody>
		<table colsep="1" frame="none" outputclass="formatc_none" rowsep="1" id="e02516">
			<tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="1">
				<colspec colname="col1" colnum="1" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<colspec colname="col2" colnum="2" colsep="0" colwidth="50*"/>
				<tbody>
					<row rowsep="1">
						<entry colname="col1">
							<fig id="e02517">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV035310.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02518"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
						<entry colname="col2">
							<fig id="e02519">
								<figgroup>
									<image href="../../images/OOV035413.eps" align="center" height="1.740in" placement="break" id="e02520"/>
								</figgroup>
							</fig>
						</entry>
					</row>
				</tbody>
			</tgroup>
		</table>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<p>Touch the icon (1) several times or keep touching it, or press down the fan speed control lever (2) several times or keep pressing it down.</p>
				<p>However, you can still operate the mode and air intake icons as long as the <term translate="no">EV</term> button is in the <term translate="no">POWER ON</term> or <term translate="no">DRIVE READY</term> position.</p>
			</li>
		</ul>
	</conbody>
